# Full EA-3 v2 feature set. (It was cut to 'emmc' during Home Assistant bring-up;
# sgx came back once confirmed on the EA3, and switch + audio are RE-ENABLED here.)
#
# !!! SIZE: `switch` and `audio` are =y in their feature fragments, and an x86_64
# EA-3 kernel already fills ~7,037,952 of CEFDK's 7,417,856-byte bootlinux window.
# =y switch+audio (on top of sgx) very likely OVERRUNS it; an oversized bzImage is
# TRUNCATED silently and does not boot. The documented fix is MODULES (=m) on p1 —
# NOT done here: the switch SPI/b53 + ASoC drivers are injected obj-y via
# board/ea/common/kernel/objs.mk (switch board glue built-in), so =m needs
# load-ordering + a build/boot measurement that cannot be done without building.
# MEASURE the bzImage before trusting a boot. `audio` has also never been built
# for x86_64 (compile risk); its platform driver is probe-only (enable_pcm=0,
# reading TX reg 0x2004 hangs the SoC).
#
# Shared EA feature sets this board pulls in. One word per feature, space
# separated. Each lives in board/ea/common/features/<name>/, holding both its
# halves: defconfig (userspace) and linux.fragment (kernel).
#   wifi  - Atheros ath9k radio + wpa_supplicant/iw userspace
#   emmc  - sdhci-pci + ext4, persistent rootfs on mmcblk0p1
#   switch - BCM53125 managed switch over SPI (DSA/b53); gives lan1/lan2
#   sgx    - PowerVR SGX545 kernel driver (3D); gives /dev/dri/card0
#   audio  - CE5300 I2S + ADAU1451 codec, ALSA, AirPlay (shairport-sync)
#            and Spotify Connect (librespot)
emmc sgx switch audio
